  "subtitle_text": "1\n00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,050\nThe James Webb Space Telescope floats in deep space, its golden mirrors\n\n2\n00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:10,100\nfacing the cosmic dark. Infrared deep-field images reveal galaxies that formed more\n\n3\n00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:15,151\nthan thirteen billion years ago. These images show how early galaxies assembled\n\n4\n00:00:15,151 --> 00:00:20,201\nfrom gas and dark matter after the Big Bang. Infrared light pierces\n\n5\n00:00:20,201 --> 00:00:25,251\ncosmic dust, unveiling hidden star-forming nurseries inside a glowing nebula. The findings\n\n6\n00:00:25,251 --> 00:00:30,301\nchallenge older models of how spiral galaxies grew so quickly in the\n\n7\n00:00:30,301 --> 00:00:35,352\nearly cosmos. This evolving universe still hides secrets that new observatories are\n\n8\n00:00:35,352 --> 00:00:40,402\nonly beginning to unlock.\n",
